{"step_index":871,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T18:29:09Z","thinking":"Sidebar, header, and various text elements are primary candidates for light-mode theming, potentially turning white. The text elements could be styled with a dark color. Identifying these elements is crucial to determining the application's light mode styling.\n\n\nObserved that specific UI elements, including inputs, dropdowns, expanders, and radio button labels, exhibit light-mode theming. Hypothesized that applying a global CSS override with `!important` would enforce a cyber-dark theme regardless of user or browser settings. The initial CSS block focuses on theming the sidebar, header, and typography. Further CSS rules will target and style the input elements and dropdowns, with color overrides to match the desired dark theme.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Add theme-lock CSS rules in app.py to prevent light mode glitched styling","EndLine":265,"Instruction":"Add theme locking and input styling to CSS","ReplacementContent":"    /* Sliders */\n    .stSlider [data-baseweb=\"slider\"] {\n        margin-top: 4px;\n    }\n\n    /* Lock Sidebar, Header & Surfaces to Cyber Dark regardless of browser theme */\n    [data-testid=\"stSidebar\"] {\n        background-color: #060b18 !important;\n        border-right: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15) !important;\n    }\n    [data-testid=\"stSidebar\"] * {\n        color: #cbd5e1;\n    }\n    [data-testid=\"stHeader\"] {\n        background: rgba(3, 7, 18, 0.7) !important;\n        backdrop-filter: blur(12px) !important;\n    }\n\n    /* Typography & Text Visibility Lock */\n    p, span, label, [data-testid=\"stMarkdownContainer\"] p, [data-testid=\"stCaptionContainer\"] {\n        color: #cbd5e1 !important;\n    }\n    [data-testid=\"stCaptionContainer\"] {\n        color: #94a3b8 !important;\n    }\n    strong, b {\n        color: #f8fa