{"step_index":878,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T18:29:29Z","content":"I have fixed the issue where the interface appeared distorted or unreadable when the browser or system was set to Light mode.\n\n---\n\n### Root Cause\nWhen Streamlit runs on a machine with a light mode preference, default browser styling attempts to inject light backgrounds (`#ffffff`), dark gray text (`#31333F`), and white input boxes, creating clashing white-on-white text, invisible labels, and fragmented containers.\n\n---\n\n### Fixes Applied\n\n1. **Strict Theme Enclosure in [`.streamlit/config.toml`](file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/.streamlit/config.toml)**:\n   - Locked the base theme to `dark` with designated cyber backgrounds (`#030712`, `#0b1121`) and high-contrast text (`#f8fafc`).\n\n2. **Universal CSS Overrides in [`app.py`](file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/app.py)**:\n   - **Sidebar & Header**: Locked to dark frosted surfaces (`#060b18`, `rgba(3, 7, 18, 0.7)`), preventing them from turning bright white.\n   - **Text & Labels**: Explicitly forced all paragraphs, labels, captions, and metrics to high-contrast cyber tones (`#cbd5e1`, `#f8fafc`, `#94a3b8`).\n   - **Inputs, Selectboxes & Menus**: Styled all text boxes, sliders, file dropzones, and dropdown menus with dark frosted slate backgrounds (`#0b1329`) and cyan border halos.\n   - **Expanders & Radios**: Ensured expander summaries and radio options maintain clean neon visibility.\n\nThe UI will now render with consistent contrast and styling across all browser and OS theme settings."}
